:"for each iteration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The batched sequence listens to the subject without owning it: when the batched sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends or is cancelled, its wait ends at once and the subject stays pending for its other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"awaiters. A subject sent an error ends the batched sequence with that error, except"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" (as when another awaiter cancels the subject): then the signal stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"firing and the batches go on. A subject sent a value before iteration begins fires when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signal’s task starts, which may come after elements have arrived, so the first batch may be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"short. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy listens anew, so a subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already sent a value fires again when a later batched sequence’s signal task starts."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","text":"Example"},{"code":["let shutdown = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","for try await messages in inbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(50), .signal(shutdown))) {","    store(messages)","}","\/\/ Elsewhere: flush whatever is pending before shutting down.","try shutdown.send()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/eitherbatchstrategy\/signal(_:)-ommi"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes once, when the given subject is sent a value."}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/b